      <activity id="381353b4-a5a8-5e8c-a27b-74ca678067e2" activityNameId="d3eab273-aba4-5448-9502-eadd45551ccc" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xxx Softwood, Scandinavian, standing, under bark, in forest</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xxx Softwood, Scandinavian, standing, under bark, in forest
The volume does not include the bark. CO2 assimilation is based on 49.4% carbon in the wood. Biomass energy equals gross calorific value including bark.;
UUID: 43f83ccf-e697-3e15-b9a0-0194557dda7c
This module includes the CO2 absorption from air and the land-use for the trees to grow. Forest road area is not included in the land use.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Natural growth. Relates to the forest area and CO2 from air needed to produce spruce. It is assumed that other softwood species need similar time and area to grow.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_43f83ccf-e697-3e15-b9a0-0194557dda7c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
